; TEST: abort=1 c-emit-exit=4
;
; `rem u32 %x 0` with the divisor an INLINE IMMEDIATE: the zero-divisor
; check is the same two lines for `rem` as for `div` (trap_div_zero.ir),
; and it has to be, because the remainder of a division that does not
; happen is not a number either. Kind 1, the shared `bfausr_trap`.
;
; The immediate spelling is the point of having this fixture beside
; trap_div_zero.ir: the divisor reaches rcx through
; __bfa_emit_operand_text's literal arm rather than a slot, and a lowering
; that only emitted the check on the slot path would pass one of the two.
;
; If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; Mutation (run): the `test`/`jz` pair dropped -> SIGFPE (signal 8), which
; is neither this tree's numeric trap nor the expected SIGILL.
;
; `c-emit-exit=4`: the C backend refuses `rem` by name (c-backend.md D4
; row 5).

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u32 4000000000
%2 = rem u32 %1 0
%3 = iconst u8 7
ret %3
}
